               <p xml:id="idm208">In August 1883 Niels W. Gade asked Hartmann to write a piece to be performed in Musikforeningen in celebration of Martin Luther's four hundredth anniversary that year. Hartmann consulted his friend Nicolai Bøgh concerning the choice of text or text author. He decided in favour of Johan Ludvig Heiberg's poem "I Saxernes Land" (1841) from "Cantate ved Universitets Fest i Anledning af Reformationens Indførelse", with music by C.E.F. Weyse. Hartmann's cantata was not finished until 1884.</p>
            </history>
